    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6417" root="جنب" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَنِبٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَنِبَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  It is also applied as an
epithet to a wolf, because he pretends to halt,
from guile, or cunning. (L, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also A man
<i>who goes aside,</i> or <i>to a distance, from the beaten
way, for fear of guests' coming to him for entertainment.</i> (K, TA.)

